generate_block_port_connection1.sv

^\[main\.p0\] always main\.y == main\.x: PROVED .*$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
Fails with "unknown identifier G". To be tackled once both #2101
(hierarchical references into named generate blocks) and #2186 (interface
ports take the parameters of the bound instance) have been merged: #2101
alone makes G[0].a work in expressions, but not as a port connection. The
interface port actuals that #2186 resolves are plain identifiers only, and
the scope symbols of named generate blocks that #2101 adds are created
after the module instances have been parameterized.
